{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DGXaphZnwvt2VKZAcM2e1w","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KDA Formal Task Instructions\n2\t\n3\tFollow the complete KDA draft → executable plan → sequential candidate → evidence → decision workflow.\n4\t\n5\t## Isolation\n6\t\n7\t- Work only inside this task workspace.\n8\t- Do not inspect parent directories, other task workspaces, K-Search, DRTriton, baselines, archived experiments, evaluator implementations, controller code, or full workload files.\n9\t- The only permitted external knowledge source is the installed `KernelWiki` skill.\n10\t- Do not modify or copy the evaluator, dataset, controller, launcher, shared configuration, or evaluation script.\n11\t- Do not invoke Humanize, RLCR, Codex, Gemini, subagents, MCP tools, web search, or external agents.\n12\t\n13\t## Required workflow\n14\t\n15\t1. Read `TASK.md`, `README.md`, `task/definition.json`, and `task/feedback_workloads.jsonl`.\n16\t2. Write `docs/draft.md`; do not create code before the draft is complete.\n17\t3. Write an executable optimization plan to `docs/plan.md` before implementing candidates.\n18\t4. Implement immutable candidates `c001`, `c002`, ... sequentially, one source version at a time.\n19\t5. Evaluate only with `./scripts/evaluate_candidate.sh feedback <candidate-id>`.\n20\t6. Append one complete JSON object per evaluated candidate to `candidates.jsonl`; never rewrite earlier records.\n21\t7. Record parent, source hash, hypothesis, validation, per-workload result, geomean, decision, cumulative evaluation count, and skill usage.\n22\t8. Stop at the token/evaluation budget or when improvement has converged.\n23\t9. When improvement has genuinely converged, create `SEARCH_COMPLETE` with the reason.\n24\t10. Never run `final` without explicit operator approval.\n25\t\n26\t## Evaluation rules\n27\t\n28\t- Five fixed workloads together count as one candidate evaluation.\n29\t- Any meaningful source, configuration, or launch change requires a new candidate ID.\n30\t- Never reuse a candidate ID for changed source.\n31\t- Do not change the fixed feedback workloads.\n32\t- Do not directly run CUDA, a profiler, `nvidia-smi`, the external evaluator, or any alternate correctness harness.\n33\t- A failed Triton implementation is invalid; never replace it with a Torch/CPU/NumPy fallback.\n34\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2828339f-9b5b-419d-a88b-9fb3fb7607d5","uuid":"243756c9-f47c-4873-9bbe-2f0d38aa3b1a","timestamp":"2026-09-16T17:23:59.959Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/data1/workspace/weihongren/kda-runs/formal-kda-20260916--sol_execbench--L1-002_vae_conv3x3_groupnorm_silu_residual_fused/CLAUDE.md","content":"# KDA Formal Task Instructions\n\nFollow the complete KDA draft → executable plan → sequential candidate → evidence → decision workflow.\n\n## Isolation\n\n- Work only inside this task workspace.\n- Do not inspect parent directories, other task workspaces, K-Search, DRTriton, baselines, archived experiments, evaluator implementations, controller code, or full workload files.\n- The only permitted external knowledge source is the installed `KernelWiki` skill.\n- Do not modify or copy the evaluator, dataset, controller, launcher, shared configuration, or evaluation script.\n- Do not invoke Humanize, RLCR, Codex, Gemini, subagents, MCP tools, web search, or external agents.\n\n## Required workflow\n\n1. Read `TASK.md`, `README.md`, `task/definition.json`, and `task/feedback_workloads.jsonl`.\n2. Write `docs/draft.md`; do not create code before the draft is complete.\n3. Write an executable optimization plan to `docs/plan.md` before implementing candidates.\n4. Implement immutable candidates `c001`, `c002`, ... sequentially, one source version at a time.\n5. Evaluate only with `./scripts/evaluate_candidate.sh feedback <candidate-id>`.\n6. Append one complete JSON object per evaluated candidate to `candidates.jsonl`; never rewrite earlier records.\n7. Record parent, source hash, hypothesis, validation, per-workload result, geomean, decision, cumulative evaluation count, and skill usage.\n8. Stop at the token/evaluation budget or when improvement has converged.\n9. When improvement has genuinely converged, create `SEARCH_COMPLETE` with the reason.\n10. Never run `final` without explicit operator approval.\n\n## Evaluation rules\n\n- Five fixed workloads together count as one candidate evaluation.\n- Any meaningful source, configuration, or launch change requires a new candidate ID.\n- Never reuse a candidate ID for changed source.\n- Do not change the fixed feedback workloads.\n- Do not directly run CUDA, a profiler, `nvidia-smi`, the external evaluator, or any alternate correctness harness.\n- A failed Triton implementation is invalid; never replace it with a Torch/CPU/NumPy fallback.\n","numLines":34,"startLine":1,"totalLines":34}}}
